**(b) Scope creep beyond the spec**

1. **`AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` exemption** — confirmed present in `scripts/validate-okf.ts`'s `EXEMPT_FILES`, in `scripts/validate-okf.test.ts` ("root AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are exempt"), and documented in `docs/agents/domain.md` ("`AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/skills/**`..."). The spec's exemption list only says: *"any `README.md` at any depth, `docs/index.md`, `docs/agents/diataxis-context.md` ... everything under `.claude/skills/`, `.agents/skills/`, `.sandcastle/`, plus build/vendor output."* AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md are nowhere in that list. This is undocumented-by-the-spec scope creep in the exemption surface — but it is *not* a doc/code mismatch, since domain.md, the validator, and the tests all agree with each other. Neither file carries a `type` field or any frontmatter, so without this exemption they'd fail validation.
